1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,436
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:10,701
I'm arresting you for the murder

3
00:00:10,811 --> 00:00:13,280
of the boy you blew up
under the Crown Point Bridge.

4
00:00:13,614 --> 00:00:15,742
You blew that kid sky-high.

5
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:19,251
You are lying! You
are a lying traitor!

6
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:23,724
I need you at the
head of the GCPD.

7
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,917
Let them think you're a hero.

8
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:27,854
GORDON: I screwed up, Harv.

9
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:31,363
Sofia hired the Pyg.
And I covered it up.

10
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:35,195
SOFIA: <i>We all have
to make sacrifices.</i>

11
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:36,609
<i>Thought i was all about family.</i>

12
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:38,203
Never said it was
a happy family.

13
00:00:39,006 --> 00:00:40,804
(SCREAMING)

14
00:00:41,742 --> 00:00:43,802
My friend thinks
we're here to rob you.

15
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:46,443
<i>But I know you torture plants</i>

16
00:00:46,547 --> 00:00:49,346
<i>- in the name of science, Roland Charles.</i>
- (GRUNTS)

17
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:57,689
Lee Thompkins may have made
Ed strong, but I see the other you.

18
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:00,218
<i>- The Riddler.</i>
- (NYGMA LAUGHING)

19
00:01:00,294 --> 00:01:01,592
I'm back.

20
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,500
(LAUGHING)

21
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:15,941
(MAN COUGHS)

22
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:19,109
(MAN CONTINUES LAUGHING)

23
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:27,244
(MAN LAUGHING BOISTEROUSLY)

24
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:33,720
(MAN CLEARS THROAT)

25
00:01:43,537 --> 00:01:44,630
(MAN COUGHS)

26
00:01:54,915 --> 00:01:55,915
(GRUNTS)

27
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,284
(SIGHS)

28
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:05,958
(MAN CONTINUES LAUGHING)

29
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:07,789
(GAS HISSING)

30
00:02:20,841 --> 00:02:22,309
(SNIFFING)

31
00:02:23,543 --> 00:02:24,875
What's that smell?

32
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:26,312
(SNIFFING)

33
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:39,584
(SNIFFING)

34
00:02:48,869 --> 00:02:51,395
(MISSILE WHISTLING)

35
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:54,232
(MEN SCREAMING)

36
00:02:57,577 --> 00:02:59,409
(ALARMS SOUNDING)

37
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,215
Uncle Penguin
sent me to get you.

38
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:15,822
Come on, let's get ice cream.

39
00:03:25,505 --> 00:03:26,996
(BLOWS LANDING)

40
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:30,676
The Narrows is under
new management.

41
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:32,569
(GRUNTING)

42
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:35,046
- The Narrows is Sampson's turf.
- (WHIMPERING)

43
00:03:36,116 --> 00:03:40,349
And Sampson... Well,
collects protection.

44
00:03:41,655 --> 00:03:43,817
And people need to
find out what happens

45
00:03:44,691 --> 00:03:45,818
when you don't pay!

46
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:47,917
(GRUNTS)

47
00:03:48,028 --> 00:03:49,929
(BOTH WHIMPERING)

48
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,264
(GUN COCKS)

49
00:03:52,933 --> 00:03:54,902
Please. My family.

50
00:03:56,203 --> 00:03:57,483
Do I look like an animal to you?

51
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:00,868
I wouldn't hurt your family.

52
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:05,104
(BOTH SCREAMING)

53
00:04:05,212 --> 00:04:07,113
Unless they don't pay me!

54
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,716
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

55
00:04:16,056 --> 00:04:17,922
GORDON: Before Don Falcone died,

56
00:04:18,525 --> 00:04:21,552
he warned me, I had no idea
what I'd brought to the city.

57
00:04:22,462 --> 00:04:24,658
I now know he was
talking about the Pyg.

58
00:04:25,799 --> 00:04:26,960
Somebody must've told him.

59
00:04:27,901 --> 00:04:32,134
My guess, that person has evidence
that links Sofia to the Pyg's murders.

60
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:34,306
Why not come forward
with what you know?

61
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,933
It has to be more than
just my word against hers.

62
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:39,570
Or are you afraid the truth is
going to drag you down, too?

63
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:43,140
- Oh, Harvey, we've been over this.
- When did you know?

64
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:47,085
I swear, I had no idea
until after it was too late.

65
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:49,988
Now, you can be pissed, but
this is bigger than both of us.

66
00:04:58,198 --> 00:04:59,632
I need to know I
can count on you.

67
00:05:03,537 --> 00:05:04,537
Yeah, Jim.

68
00:05:07,274 --> 00:05:08,765
I'll help you take down Sofia.

69
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:12,971
But then you're gonna have
to pay for what you've done.

70
00:05:13,914 --> 00:05:15,246
I personally guarantee it.

71
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:20,148
I know an ex-Falcone assassin.
Might have beans to spill.

72
00:05:20,253 --> 00:05:22,449
Went by the name "the
Scandinavian Skinner."

73
00:05:22,756 --> 00:05:25,453
Sit tight. I have
history with the Skinner.

74
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:29,695
(DOOR CLOSES)

75
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:34,724
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

76
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:55,679
SELINA: You know, you
have, like, no food in here, right?

77
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:57,790
BRUCE: Selina?

78
00:05:59,259 --> 00:06:01,421
What are you doing here?
What's... What's wrong?

79
00:06:02,062 --> 00:06:04,502
SELINA: Why does something
have to be wrong for me to come by?

80
00:06:05,165 --> 00:06:06,165
Seriously?

81
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:12,263
I need help. (SIGHS)

82
00:06:14,241 --> 00:06:15,241
You mean money.

83
00:06:16,343 --> 00:06:20,075
(SIGHS) I stole something,
fenced it, now I want to get it back.

84
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,877
And I'd steal it, but
the fence is difficult.

85
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:25,314
So, I need money.

86
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:28,188
Why don't you just ask
Barbara Kean for the money?

87
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:29,780
'Cause I don't wanna
get her involved.

88
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,418
Look, I'll pay you back.

89
00:06:31,524 --> 00:06:34,050
I just don't have time because
if the fence sells what I...

90
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:35,671
But you still haven't told me
why you wanna get it back.

91
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:38,529
Because it's what I stole
from Roland Charles.

92
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,895
- The Wayne scientist...
- That Ivy killed.

93
00:06:45,772 --> 00:06:47,035
(SELINA SIGHS)

94
00:06:47,107 --> 00:06:49,167
I didn't know she was
gonna do that, Bruce.

95
00:06:49,776 --> 00:06:51,574
(STUTTERS) And I just...

96
00:06:52,112 --> 00:06:53,112
You feel bad.

97
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:58,116
Look, if you don't wanna help
me, then I'll just find another way.

98
00:06:58,218 --> 00:06:59,218
Let me get some cash.

99
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:03,461
There's oatmeal raisin
cookies in the blue tin.

100
00:07:12,666 --> 00:07:14,225
(BUZZER SOUNDING)

101
00:07:14,301 --> 00:07:15,792
Why are you dragging me here?

102
00:07:16,036 --> 00:07:17,036
(BARKS)

103
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:18,938
Cobblepot.

104
00:07:20,573 --> 00:07:22,906
A guy called. Wanted
me to give you a message.

105
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:26,473
Finally! (EXHALES)

106
00:07:29,482 --> 00:07:32,509
"I can lend you a hand,
but you won't find me helpful.

107
00:07:33,086 --> 00:07:36,250
"My name may sound tasty,
but the flavor is dreadful."

108
00:07:39,693 --> 00:07:41,025
Is it "knuckle sandwich"?

109
00:07:42,595 --> 00:07:44,291
- (CHUCKLES) Yeah.
- No.

110
00:07:52,072 --> 00:07:54,337
- (MUSIC PLAYING ON SPEAKERS)
- (KIDS GIGGLING)

111
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:58,477
Hello, Agnes.

112
00:08:00,413 --> 00:08:02,541
Or should I say, "the Skinner"?

113
00:08:05,118 --> 00:08:06,780
Detective Bullock.

114
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,213
I don't go by that name anymore.

115
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:11,121
I'm retired.

116
00:08:12,025 --> 00:08:15,359
- You kids, don't spoil your dinner.
- Okay, Grandma.

117
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:18,697
I'm looking for someone

118
00:08:18,798 --> 00:08:21,768
who might've been Don Falcone's
eyes and ears when he was down south.

119
00:08:22,135 --> 00:08:23,467
Why would I tell you that?

120
00:08:24,304 --> 00:08:25,431
Because we have history.

121
00:08:25,805 --> 00:08:28,832
That history got me
four years in the gulag.

122
00:08:30,043 --> 00:08:31,170
Either you help me,

123
00:08:32,612 --> 00:08:34,123
or I tell your beautiful
grandchildren

124
00:08:34,147 --> 00:08:36,673
how their meemaw
used to skin people alive.

125
00:08:38,685 --> 00:08:40,677
Hey, kids, you wanna
hear a really funny story?

126
00:08:40,754 --> 00:08:42,732
All right. No, it's all right.
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

127
00:08:42,756 --> 00:08:43,756
HARVEY: Never mind.

128
00:08:46,059 --> 00:08:50,190
Falcone only really
trusted the bookkeeper.

129
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,492
The one who always
smelled of fish.

130
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,431
- Mr. Penn?
- Yeah.

131
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:58,270
Penn.

132
00:08:58,772 --> 00:09:02,209
And good luck finding
him. I heard he vanished.

133
00:09:02,776 --> 00:09:03,776
Poof.

134
00:09:06,746 --> 00:09:09,045
(GRUNTS ANGRILY)
How is Martin gone?

135
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:12,045
(PANTS)

136
00:09:12,152 --> 00:09:13,152
Never mind.

137
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:14,980
Penguin is coming.

138
00:09:15,688 --> 00:09:17,919
Go to Arkham and kill him now.

139
00:09:18,425 --> 00:09:19,425
Okey-dokey.

140
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:20,870
- Oh, by the way...
- (DOOR OPENS)

141
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:22,371
a buddy of mine just
got out of the hospital.

142
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:23,395
He's looking for work.

143
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:25,058
You mind if he tags along?

144
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:28,700
Hiya.

145
00:09:33,339 --> 00:09:36,207
Just make sure Penguin
dies choking on his own blood.

146
00:09:38,378 --> 00:09:40,040
HARVEY: Why is
Cobblepot in the infirmary?

147
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:43,307
Heard he mouthed off to a guard,
then slipped and hit his head.

148
00:09:49,489 --> 00:09:50,889
(GASPS)

149
00:09:50,957 --> 00:09:52,949
Bullock. This is a surprise.

150
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,128
Hey, Oswald. Good
to see you, too.

151
00:09:55,628 --> 00:09:58,564
I just had a few questions
about a former employee of yours.

152
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:00,557
- (WOMAN SCREAMING)
- (GASPS)

153
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:01,896
WOMAN: They got guns!

154
00:10:02,502 --> 00:10:03,502
Open that door!

155
00:10:05,171 --> 00:10:06,764
(PANICKED CHATTERING)

156
00:10:09,976 --> 00:10:11,444
GUARD: Everybody, split up.

157
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:16,909
HARVEY: Get out
of the way. Clear out!

158
00:10:17,584 --> 00:10:18,643
Move, move, move!

159
00:10:19,819 --> 00:10:20,819
Hey!

160
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:24,789
You two, don't come any closer.

161
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:26,391
ZSASZ: Bullock?

162
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:29,421
Dude, I thought you
stopped being a cop.

163
00:10:30,597 --> 00:10:31,637
Guess it didn't take, huh?

164
00:10:32,265 --> 00:10:33,265
Not so much.

165
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:37,493
- You remember Wendell, don't you?
- Howdy.

166
00:10:37,704 --> 00:10:40,037
I don't know why you two
are here, and I don't care.

167
00:10:41,007 --> 00:10:42,007
Walk away!

168
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:44,600
See, I'm afraid
we can't do that.

169
00:10:45,278 --> 00:10:46,541
(WEAPON WHIRRING)

170
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,781
We're not leaving here
without the Penguin.

171
00:10:54,454 --> 00:10:56,946
ZSASZ: Harvey.
Do yourself a favor,

172
00:10:57,457 --> 00:11:02,020
give us Penguin, and live to
get drunk another day. Hmm?

173
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:04,721
As tempting as that sounds, no.

174
00:11:05,298 --> 00:11:07,028
- (BELL RINGING)
- (ALARM BLARING)

175
00:11:11,704 --> 00:11:12,948
GUARD 1: Come
on, let's go. Let's go.

176
00:11:12,972 --> 00:11:14,600
(GUARDS CLAMORING)

177
00:11:16,142 --> 00:11:17,371
It's okay.

178
00:11:17,944 --> 00:11:19,139
We'll come back.

179
00:11:19,979 --> 00:11:23,006
GUARD 2: He's escaped.
Oswald Cobblepot has escaped.

180
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:25,680
(CLAMORING CONTINUES)

181
00:11:25,785 --> 00:11:26,844
(WHISTLE BLOWING)

182
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,282
(PANICKED CHATTERING
AND SCREAMING)

183
00:11:33,459 --> 00:11:35,291
- (WHIMPERING)
- (GUNSHOTS)

184
00:11:43,336 --> 00:11:44,565
(TIRES SCREECHING)

185
00:11:46,272 --> 00:11:47,331
Nygma.

186
00:11:49,576 --> 00:11:50,576
BRUCE: What?

187
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:53,411
You're just different.

188
00:11:54,414 --> 00:11:55,507
Different how?

189
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,950
You were a complete
douchebag to me at the club.

190
00:11:59,953 --> 00:12:02,616
And now you're not.

191
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:06,426
Listen, Selina,
about that night...

192
00:12:06,526 --> 00:12:10,122
Oh, no, you're not going to
try to apologize to me, are you?

193
00:12:11,064 --> 00:12:12,362
No, I just wanted to say...

194
00:12:12,432 --> 00:12:13,491
Save it.

195
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:18,705
Because you are probably going to
be a douchebag to me later anyway.

196
00:12:22,709 --> 00:12:23,709
Missed you, too.

197
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:33,284
Kitty Cat, back so soon?

198
00:12:34,454 --> 00:12:35,454
'Sup, Floyd?

199
00:12:39,058 --> 00:12:41,618
I'm gonna need that stuff I
brought to you the other day.

200
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:42,761
FLOYD: Oh.

201
00:12:44,964 --> 00:12:46,159
You mean this stuff?

202
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:48,565
The stuff you tried to
break in and steal last night?

203
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:52,436
You think I wouldn't
check the camera?

204
00:12:52,739 --> 00:12:53,739
Great.

205
00:12:54,941 --> 00:12:56,967
You remember what I said
about being a douchebag?

206
00:12:59,846 --> 00:13:01,781
I'll pay double
what you gave me.

207
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,139
This your bank?

208
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,920
How about I take the money

209
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,221
and I keep your stuff?

210
00:13:15,094 --> 00:13:16,255
(ALL GRUNTING)

211
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:31,842
(GUNSHOT)

212
00:13:31,944 --> 00:13:32,944
Next time...

213
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:35,679
- (GRUNTS)
- take the deal.

214
00:13:41,287 --> 00:13:42,812
(GRUNTS) Got it.

215
00:13:46,959 --> 00:13:50,123
I knew that as soon as I rescued
Martin that she'd send her hitmen.

216
00:13:51,564 --> 00:13:52,564
How is Martin?

217
00:13:53,132 --> 00:13:55,363
Snug as a bug in a rug.
Here, will you hold this?

218
00:13:56,302 --> 00:13:57,822
So, do you wanna
know how I found him?

219
00:13:58,705 --> 00:14:02,335
So it turns out, Zsasz,
huge fan of the disco.

220
00:14:02,408 --> 00:14:05,674
- So I dress up as an old Polish...
- Perhaps another time!

221
00:14:05,745 --> 00:14:09,307
Now that Martin is safe, we
need to focus on killing Sofia.

222
00:14:09,382 --> 00:14:10,680
We need a power base.

223
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:13,515
I know. That's why we're here.

224
00:14:15,555 --> 00:14:16,887
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

225
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,160
Hello. (CHUCKLES)

226
00:14:23,963 --> 00:14:26,125
Ed. You're back.

227
00:14:26,632 --> 00:14:28,157
- Mmm-hmm.
- How are you doing?

228
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:31,968
Worlds better.
Honestly, thank you.

229
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:36,372
Oh, no. What
happened to your hand?

230
00:14:37,343 --> 00:14:38,641
Sofia Falcone.

231
00:14:39,979 --> 00:14:43,074
Smashed it with a hammer, and
then threw me out on the street.

232
00:14:43,416 --> 00:14:45,476
And put Sampson in
charge of The Narrows.

233
00:14:46,152 --> 00:14:47,245
I see.

234
00:14:47,353 --> 00:14:49,720
But together, we can
get that bitch back.

235
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:52,830
Show her that she can't just
take everything we've built.

236
00:14:52,925 --> 00:14:54,518
Yeah, Oswald, she can't help.

237
00:14:56,429 --> 00:14:57,429
LEE: What is this?

238
00:14:58,931 --> 00:15:00,559
What is going on?
What's wrong with you?

239
00:15:01,934 --> 00:15:05,462
I let him out of his cage, and he,
in turn, helped me get out of mine.

240
00:15:07,373 --> 00:15:08,373
You're him.

241
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,075
The Riddler.

242
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:11,610
(CHUCKLES)

243
00:15:12,111 --> 00:15:13,111
Hi, Lee.

244
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:16,425
You know, I was really hoping that
you were still running The Narrows,

245
00:15:16,449 --> 00:15:17,542
maybe could help us, but...

246
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:20,752
Guess not.

247
00:15:20,853 --> 00:15:22,453
Yeah, so what's your
next brilliant idea?

248
00:15:22,522 --> 00:15:24,957
Sofia will have turned Falcone
Mansion into a stronghold.

249
00:15:25,057 --> 00:15:26,923
It will be impossible
to get at her.

250
00:15:27,026 --> 00:15:29,222
Oswald, you think I
don't have a backup plan?

251
00:15:30,029 --> 00:15:32,149
I'm gonna have Victor
Fries put you in a block of ice.

252
00:15:32,532 --> 00:15:35,593
I'm gonna take you to Sofia
like a chilly Trojan horse,

253
00:15:35,802 --> 00:15:37,600
- pretend to hand you over...
- (CHUCKLES)

254
00:15:39,138 --> 00:15:40,538
Are you kidding me?

255
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,203
It's a fantastic plan.

256
00:15:43,409 --> 00:15:44,409
Try again!

257
00:15:44,477 --> 00:15:46,605
All right, let me help.

258
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,224
Look, all of your capos have
pledged their loyalty to Sofia...

259
00:15:49,248 --> 00:15:50,511
Do you think I can't handle it?

260
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:51,945
I know you can't.

261
00:15:52,018 --> 00:15:53,418
Look what she did to me.

262
00:15:53,686 --> 00:15:55,587
I will pull the trigger
on that bitch myself.

263
00:15:55,755 --> 00:15:58,122
That's some tough tongue,
but we both know that's just talk.

264
00:15:58,191 --> 00:15:59,784
Enough! Both of you.

265
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:02,754
If we wanna fight
Sofia, we need muscle.

266
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:04,463
I agree.

267
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:07,959
I can tell you where to look.

268
00:16:10,336 --> 00:16:11,634
Don't you think he misses you?

269
00:16:15,508 --> 00:16:16,806
Who... Who is she talking about?

270
00:16:21,414 --> 00:16:23,645
NYGMA: Grundy!

271
00:16:24,450 --> 00:16:25,816
You down here, big fella?

272
00:16:26,285 --> 00:16:28,015
Your best friend and pal,

273
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:30,486
Edward Nygma.

274
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:34,760
Hey, guess what?
I'm smart again!

275
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,792
(WATER LAPPING)

276
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:42,867
There he is.

277
00:16:43,369 --> 00:16:45,634
Pale skin, nobody upstairs...

278
00:16:45,705 --> 00:16:46,866
Who's my buddy?

279
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:50,006
Correct. You.

280
00:16:50,610 --> 00:16:51,634
Oh, boy.

281
00:16:51,711 --> 00:16:53,509
So, we're corralling allies.

282
00:16:53,579 --> 00:16:55,741
Penguin and I are going
to kill Sofia Falcone.

283
00:16:55,848 --> 00:17:00,377
And we need a big galoot like you for
cannon fodder. How does that sound?

284
00:17:01,587 --> 00:17:02,987
(GRUNTING SOFTLY)

285
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:06,730
What's your problem? Why
are you looking at me like that?

286
00:17:08,094 --> 00:17:09,255
- (GASPS)
- (GRUNTS)

287
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:10,362
Oh, dear.

288
00:17:10,429 --> 00:17:12,591
You're not the only
one who got smart.

289
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:16,029
Okay, Butch, I helped you.

290
00:17:16,602 --> 00:17:17,934
You remember?

291
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,266
Hot, hot arm.

292
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:21,170
Yeah, Ed put out fire.

293
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,175
But you're not Ed anymore.

294
00:17:23,242 --> 00:17:24,242
(GRUNTS)

295
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:25,709
And I'm not Grundy.

296
00:17:31,317 --> 00:17:32,517
PENGUIN: Where the hell is Ed?

297
00:17:32,585 --> 00:17:33,585
LEE: He'll be here.

298
00:17:34,353 --> 00:17:37,152
No. No, he's betrayed me, too.

299
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:39,419
I know it. I never
should have trusted him!

300
00:17:40,092 --> 00:17:41,092
Calm down.

301
00:17:41,494 --> 00:17:42,774
No, do not tell me to calm down.

302
00:17:42,862 --> 00:17:44,888
You have no idea
what I've been through!

303
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,726
Calm down! Ed will be here.

304
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:50,868
He will bring Grundy, and
we will make Sofia pay.

305
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,135
I can't wait any longer.

306
00:18:02,148 --> 00:18:04,259
HARVEY: How did Nygma get
in touch with Penguin anyway?

307
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:05,307
GORDON: I don't know.

308
00:18:05,418 --> 00:18:06,943
Nothing's ever
easy with you, is it?

309
00:18:07,053 --> 00:18:09,648
It's always like, "Find Lee,
and then she'll point us to Ed.

310
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,155
"And then we'll find Penguin,

311
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:13,283
"and he'll tell us
where to find Penn."

312
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,252
Or we could just talk
to Oswald right now.

313
00:18:16,329 --> 00:18:17,329
What?

314
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:20,631
- (GLASS SHATTERS)
- MAN: Hey, you son of a...

315
00:18:20,967 --> 00:18:21,967
(PENGUIN GRUNTING)

316
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:23,902
What are you doing here?

317
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:28,132
We're looking for an Arkham escapee
about yea tall, walks with a limp,

318
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,401
mommy complex?

319
00:18:30,977 --> 00:18:34,106
Those trumped-up charges
you used to put me away

320
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:35,905
have lost their teeth.

321
00:18:35,982 --> 00:18:39,248
- Martin is still alive.
- So produce him.

322
00:18:39,318 --> 00:18:41,116
PENGUIN: Nope. He is not safe

323
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:45,419
until Sofia Falcone has
been dealt with permanently.

324
00:18:46,626 --> 00:18:48,959
I think you and I want
the same thing, Oswald.

325
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,995
We both want Sofia to go away.

326
00:18:53,566 --> 00:18:56,365
Then turn around and walk away.

327
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,600
Let me do what I do.

328
00:18:59,338 --> 00:19:02,001
No. I want her in jail, and
for that I need evidence.

329
00:19:02,274 --> 00:19:04,266
I want your
bookkeeper, Mr. Penn.

330
00:19:05,211 --> 00:19:06,873
What would he know about...

331
00:19:09,615 --> 00:19:12,141
That little weasel
was working for her!

332
00:19:12,718 --> 00:19:17,452
Yeah, he was working for her,
for Don Falcone, everybody!

333
00:19:17,523 --> 00:19:19,617
You might want to check
your management style, pal.

334
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:20,992
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

335
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:23,828
I'm gonna kill him.

336
00:19:24,397 --> 00:19:26,366
Oswald. Oswald.

337
00:19:27,199 --> 00:19:28,531
Calm down.

338
00:19:28,768 --> 00:19:32,296
You show us where
we can find Mr. Penn,

339
00:19:33,873 --> 00:19:35,034
and I'll let you walk away.

340
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:38,510
I don't believe you.

341
00:19:38,611 --> 00:19:40,603
HARVEY: Sofia sent
Zsasz to Arkham to kill you.

342
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,447
Her goons run The Narrows.

343
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:45,383
How long do you think it's
gonna take till she finds you?

344
00:19:46,385 --> 00:19:47,853
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

345
00:19:54,293 --> 00:19:55,317
(SIGHS)

346
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:03,102
I overheard Mr. Penn talk about a place
just out of town, near the tri-corner.

347
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,534
The Spa Bosh Sumka.

348
00:20:05,571 --> 00:20:07,904
Offers special therapy.

349
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:10,567
If he's hiding, he's
probably there.

350
00:20:10,943 --> 00:20:11,943
Oswald.

351
00:20:16,348 --> 00:20:17,372
Thank you.

352
00:20:23,022 --> 00:20:25,067
That's really nice. Now, put
your hands behind your back.

353
00:20:25,091 --> 00:20:28,721
No. No! No, we had a deal!

354
00:20:28,794 --> 00:20:29,874
Harvey, what are you doing?

355
00:20:29,929 --> 00:20:31,689
If you want to look
the other way, Jim, fine.

356
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:33,495
I didn't agree to
squat. Come on.

357
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:36,866
PENGUIN: (SOBS) No! No!

358
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:46,679
- I will not forget this!
- Relax.

359
00:20:46,746 --> 00:20:48,156
If your information
on Penn is good,

360
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:50,172
at least you'll be
free of Sofia Falcone.

361
00:20:50,783 --> 00:20:51,842
ZSASZ: Well, well, well.

362
00:20:53,352 --> 00:20:56,686
Sofia's gonna be very curious to
know why you're looking for Penn.

363
00:20:57,389 --> 00:20:59,381
Hey, Penguin. Remember me?

364
00:21:00,392 --> 00:21:01,951
Oh, God, no.

365
00:21:02,561 --> 00:21:05,292
Wait, is Penn
important or something?

366
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:09,967
That's a yes. You see
that? That's his "yes" face.

367
00:21:10,069 --> 00:21:11,264
Get him in the car.

368
00:21:13,973 --> 00:21:15,737
Guess I'll have to
go dig him up myself.

369
00:21:16,642 --> 00:21:19,578
Now, you boys
want to come quietly,

370
00:21:21,347 --> 00:21:23,077
or do you want to
do it the fun way?

371
00:21:25,851 --> 00:21:27,114
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

372
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:30,253
- The fun way. Nice.
- (GUNSHOTS CONTINUE)

373
00:21:34,794 --> 00:21:36,160
(WHIMPERING)

374
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:42,499
(GUNSHOTS CONTINUE)

375
00:21:46,172 --> 00:21:47,970
- Lee.
- Shut up and get down.

376
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,140
(ENGINE STARTS)

377
00:21:49,441 --> 00:21:51,171
- (TIRES SCREECH)
- Lee?

378
00:21:59,952 --> 00:22:01,614
Come on. Let's get out of here.

379
00:22:04,623 --> 00:22:06,558
We need to get to
Penn before Zsasz does.

380
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:08,960
We need a car.

381
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:21,806
(SIGHS)

382
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,310
Migraine still?

383
00:22:25,377 --> 00:22:27,297
It's like I've been hit
in the head with a brick.

384
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:29,542
- (MUFFLED GRUNTING)
- What is that stink?

385
00:22:30,082 --> 00:22:32,074
(MUFFLED, INDISTINCT SPEAKING)

386
00:22:34,386 --> 00:22:35,445
Should've known.

387
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,123
Grundy smell like old dentures.

388
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,024
TABITHA: It's him.

389
00:22:40,526 --> 00:22:43,121
I know. I can smell him.

390
00:22:43,462 --> 00:22:45,363
- (BARBARA SNIFFING)
- Hey there, Barbara.

391
00:22:45,464 --> 00:22:46,464
(GASPS)

392
00:22:50,002 --> 00:22:51,002
Scary.

393
00:22:52,171 --> 00:22:54,003
Nygma tried to recruit
me against Sofia.

394
00:22:55,307 --> 00:22:56,331
He's working for Penguin.

395
00:22:57,076 --> 00:22:58,408
(LAUGHS)

396
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:02,579
I figured after all Ed did to you,
you should be the one to kill him.

397
00:23:06,418 --> 00:23:07,418
Wait, Butch.

398
00:23:09,855 --> 00:23:11,050
Don't just walk away again.

399
00:23:11,290 --> 00:23:14,192
Tabby, I'm gonna find a
way to get back to the old me.

400
00:23:16,295 --> 00:23:17,295
I promise.

401
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:20,358
(MUFFLED SPEAKING)

402
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,367
(GRUNTS)

403
00:23:23,369 --> 00:23:24,369
(GROANS)

404
00:23:29,875 --> 00:23:31,639
- (HIGH PITCHED RINGING)
- (GROANS)

405
00:23:33,445 --> 00:23:36,279
- (MUFFLED, DISTORTED VOICE SPEAKING)
- (BARBARA WHIMPERING SOFTLY)

406
00:23:39,051 --> 00:23:40,171
TABITHA: (ECHOES) Any ideas?

407
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,618
(GASPING)

408
00:23:43,289 --> 00:23:44,348
You okay?

409
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:46,058
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

410
00:23:46,859 --> 00:23:47,859
I'm fine.

411
00:23:49,461 --> 00:23:51,123
We send Nygma back to Sofia.

412
00:23:51,563 --> 00:23:53,361
She will torture him
to get to Penguin.

413
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:54,798
Lee has no more allies.

414
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,768
Boom, rebellion
quells, we're heroes.

415
00:23:58,137 --> 00:24:01,073
Then what about Nygma?
He just gets to walk away?

416
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:02,199
(MUFFLED SPEAKING)

417
00:24:02,474 --> 00:24:05,137
When Sofia doesn't need
him anymore, she'll kill him.

418
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:07,245
(SIGHS)

419
00:24:07,746 --> 00:24:10,238
Same end result,
none of the headache.

420
00:24:12,918 --> 00:24:15,513
Well, we did find Penguin,
but then he got away.

421
00:24:16,088 --> 00:24:18,580
So why aren't you looking for
him, instead of wasting my time?

422
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:22,928
Because I also found out that
Gordon is looking for Mr. Penn.

423
00:24:29,702 --> 00:24:31,193
Find Penn before Gordon does.

424
00:24:32,104 --> 00:24:37,099
Yeah, so, Penn, Penguin... I
mean, where are we priorities-wise?

425
00:24:38,110 --> 00:24:39,110
Do both.

426
00:24:44,984 --> 00:24:46,350
Thank you for
coming to my rescue.

427
00:24:46,452 --> 00:24:48,648
Don't bother. Without
you, I can't get to Sofia.

428
00:24:49,188 --> 00:24:50,188
Touching.

429
00:24:51,023 --> 00:24:53,652
- I cannot believe I'm doing this.
- Believe it.

430
00:24:54,259 --> 00:24:56,353
No Ed, no Grundy.
We're running out of time.

431
00:24:56,662 --> 00:24:59,689
You know this cockamamie
scheme will probably get me killed?

432
00:24:59,932 --> 00:25:02,697
If it puts Sofia in the
ground, I'm okay with that.

433
00:25:02,868 --> 00:25:04,097
(GUN COCKING)

434
00:25:05,137 --> 00:25:06,448
VICTOR: The last
time you came in here

435
00:25:06,472 --> 00:25:08,805
with one of your
schemes to regain the city,

436
00:25:10,075 --> 00:25:13,375
you promised every resource I
needed to reverse my condition.

437
00:25:17,683 --> 00:25:18,810
So, that didn't happen.

438
00:25:19,818 --> 00:25:24,153
An omission I regret, and
will rectify if given the chance.

439
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,024
Uh-huh.

440
00:25:28,193 --> 00:25:29,991
- (GAS HISSING)
- (PENGUIN YELPING)

441
00:25:31,263 --> 00:25:32,663
(INHALES DEEPLY)

442
00:25:33,399 --> 00:25:34,399
(GRUNTS)

443
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:37,365
You cannot honestly tell
me you are happy here.

444
00:25:37,936 --> 00:25:40,371
Tinkering away,
on whatever these...

445
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:42,840
Don't touch that.

446
00:25:43,675 --> 00:25:47,840
You need money for your
research, Sofia wants Penguin.

447
00:25:48,313 --> 00:25:50,407
So you deliver him to her,
you can name your price.

448
00:25:53,318 --> 00:25:54,478
VICTOR: I may have something.

449
00:25:58,924 --> 00:26:02,019
Keep this on you. It's on a timer.
Best I can do on short notice.

450
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:05,591
If being frozen affects my
brain the way it did Nygma,

451
00:26:05,697 --> 00:26:06,892
- I cannot afford...
- Ready?

452
00:26:07,099 --> 00:26:08,931
- Not yet! I...
- Don't care.

453
00:26:09,034 --> 00:26:10,559
(METAL MUSIC PLAYING)

454
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:30,920
So now you're
going to return it?

455
00:26:35,227 --> 00:26:36,718
- Selina, you said...
- Can you do it?

456
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:40,596
That's really why
you came to me.

457
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:43,561
It wasn't about the money.

458
00:26:55,047 --> 00:26:56,948
You did not kill Roland Charles.

459
00:27:01,220 --> 00:27:02,313
I was there, though.

460
00:27:05,557 --> 00:27:07,389
And what am I
supposed to say, I...

461
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:11,462
"I stole your jewelry. Sorry."

462
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:14,826
Sometimes that's enough.

463
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,773
- (DRILL WHIRRING)
- (NYGMA SCREAMING)

464
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:27,474
(GRUNTS IN PAIN)

465
00:27:28,213 --> 00:27:31,479
His strength of
mind is impressive.

466
00:27:32,384 --> 00:27:33,384
(GRUNTS)

467
00:27:38,190 --> 00:27:39,351
(SIGHS)

468
00:27:39,458 --> 00:27:41,518
You are going to tell me
where to find Penguin,

469
00:27:42,828 --> 00:27:45,855
or I will make all of this
look like a pleasant dream.

470
00:27:47,299 --> 00:27:48,494
(CHUCKLES)

471
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:49,600
Yeah, okay.

472
00:27:52,137 --> 00:27:56,006
I can be done with the teeth,
the eyes or the mind. What am I?

473
00:27:59,044 --> 00:28:02,811
I can be humorous, but
I'm never funny! (LAUGHS)

474
00:28:02,881 --> 00:28:03,881
What am I?

475
00:28:04,383 --> 00:28:05,612
(CONTINUES LAUGHING)

476
00:28:07,052 --> 00:28:08,520
(SCREAMS)

477
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:10,621
(GROANING)

478
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:11,952
Tell me where he is.

479
00:28:13,125 --> 00:28:14,821
I am telling you! (LAUGHING)

480
00:28:14,893 --> 00:28:16,828
You're just too
stupid to figure it out!

481
00:28:17,996 --> 00:28:19,430
(SCREAMING)

482
00:28:19,531 --> 00:28:22,524
- Miss Falcone, you've got a visitor.
- Kind of in the middle of something.

483
00:28:22,901 --> 00:28:23,994
Guy's got Penguin.

484
00:28:24,736 --> 00:28:25,863
(NYGMA GROANS)

485
00:28:26,838 --> 00:28:27,838
Bring him in.

486
00:28:39,418 --> 00:28:40,613
(SOFIA SCOFFS)

487
00:28:41,286 --> 00:28:43,278
(GASPS, CHUCKLES)

488
00:28:43,956 --> 00:28:45,720
Well, this is unexpected.

489
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:48,792
Heard you were
looking for Penguin.

490
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:51,591
He never was a great boss.

491
00:28:52,197 --> 00:28:53,495
Well, well, Oswald.

492
00:28:55,434 --> 00:28:56,595
Is he alive in there?

493
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:01,405
VICTOR: Maybe.

494
00:29:04,276 --> 00:29:05,505
I want $100,000.

495
00:29:08,513 --> 00:29:09,513
Pay him.

496
00:29:19,891 --> 00:29:21,091
ZSASZ: I'm not even gonna ask.

497
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:24,122
Oh, by the way, I
found out where Penn is.

498
00:29:24,463 --> 00:29:25,658
(GASPS)

499
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:32,132
Take him to the docks, shoot
him, and throw him in the river.

500
00:29:32,237 --> 00:29:33,296
(GRUNTS)

501
00:29:33,405 --> 00:29:34,429
Watch Penguin.

502
00:29:35,941 --> 00:29:36,941
Let's go get Mr. Penn.

503
00:29:45,584 --> 00:29:46,677
(KNOCKS)

504
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,783
MAN: Lovely, Miss
Gonzalez, well done.

505
00:29:56,094 --> 00:29:58,120
Pull a little harder. Right.

506
00:29:58,330 --> 00:30:00,424
That's it, Miss McGee. Come on.

507
00:30:03,168 --> 00:30:04,796
(LIVELY CHATTER AND LAUGHTER)

508
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:07,805
What fresh level
of hell is this?

509
00:30:09,441 --> 00:30:10,739
WOMAN: Who is hungry?

510
00:30:12,311 --> 00:30:13,939
(PEOPLE MIMICKING BABY NOISE)

511
00:30:15,314 --> 00:30:16,475
GCPD!

512
00:30:18,083 --> 00:30:19,608
GCPD!

513
00:30:21,019 --> 00:30:22,317
We're looking for Arthur Penn.

514
00:30:23,155 --> 00:30:24,155
What are you doing?

515
00:30:24,356 --> 00:30:26,689
Anonymity is a strict
edict here at the resort.

516
00:30:27,159 --> 00:30:28,159
I bet.

517
00:30:33,532 --> 00:30:35,626
- HARVEY: That's him.
- Penn. Penn!

518
00:30:37,636 --> 00:30:38,729
Oh, no.

519
00:30:44,242 --> 00:30:45,242
Let's take a walk.

520
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:47,845
As you were.

521
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:50,713
(PEOPLE GIGGLING AND BABBLING)

522
00:30:56,488 --> 00:30:57,854
(ICE CRACKING)

523
00:31:01,993 --> 00:31:03,985
(MUFFLED BEEPING)

524
00:31:16,007 --> 00:31:17,703
- Mr. Cobblepot.
- (SHIVERING)

525
00:31:17,809 --> 00:31:20,176
You are working for
her, too! (CHUCKLING)

526
00:31:20,245 --> 00:31:22,476
- I assure you...
- Of course you are!

527
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:24,348
Where is she?

528
00:31:24,583 --> 00:31:26,779
- You don't understand.
- (YELLS) Where is she?

529
00:31:28,387 --> 00:31:30,049
- (YELLS)
- (THE DENTIST GRUNTS)

530
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,249
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

531
00:31:35,927 --> 00:31:38,362
- Is it done?
- Sofia left before I could kill her.

532
00:31:38,697 --> 00:31:40,063
She's on her way to stop Gordon.

533
00:31:40,432 --> 00:31:43,061
<i>Meet me at the Spa Bosh
Sumka, and we will kill her together.</i>

534
00:31:53,278 --> 00:31:54,769
(GASPS)

535
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:55,939
Nygma was here?

536
00:31:57,349 --> 00:32:00,080
Miss Falcone tried to
get him to turn on you.

537
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:01,385
What?

538
00:32:01,453 --> 00:32:03,752
He endured a
tremendous amount of pain.

539
00:32:05,791 --> 00:32:06,850
He wouldn't give you up.

540
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:10,761
Where is he now?

541
00:32:11,029 --> 00:32:14,761
Her thugs took him
to the docks to kill him.

542
00:32:21,373 --> 00:32:22,602
(GRUNTS)

543
00:32:25,577 --> 00:32:30,606
I have worked for Don Falcone
for years, before Mr. Cobblepot.

544
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:33,142
When Sofia came to Gotham,

545
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:37,278
Don Falcone asked me to
keep an eye on his daughter.

546
00:32:38,023 --> 00:32:39,023
She found out.

547
00:32:39,925 --> 00:32:43,692
So you made another deal with
her, you weaselly, triple agent, you.

548
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:45,787
It's how you stay
alive in this business.

549
00:32:46,364 --> 00:32:47,855
And she let me live.

550
00:32:49,134 --> 00:32:53,128
As long as I informed to
her about Mr. Cobblepot.

551
00:32:54,539 --> 00:32:57,134
That's how she was able to
stay one step ahead of Penguin,

552
00:32:57,209 --> 00:32:58,336
with inside information.

553
00:32:58,944 --> 00:32:59,968
Then what?

554
00:33:00,078 --> 00:33:02,570
She asked me to put her in
touch with Lazlo Valentine.

555
00:33:03,281 --> 00:33:04,281
The Pyg.

556
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:06,183
So I did.

557
00:33:06,751 --> 00:33:09,084
But I told Don
Falcone right away.

558
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:11,286
All right, you're
coming with us.

559
00:33:11,356 --> 00:33:13,018
We need your
statement for the record.

560
00:33:15,093 --> 00:33:16,186
Get down!

561
00:33:16,862 --> 00:33:18,854
- (PEOPLE SCREAMING)
- (GORDON GRUNTING)

562
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:21,330
(GUNSHOTS)

563
00:33:23,335 --> 00:33:24,769
(GUNSHOTS CONTINUE)

564
00:33:37,749 --> 00:33:40,014
Get Penn out of here.
He's all that matters.

565
00:33:40,085 --> 00:33:41,815
We've got to get
you to the hospital.

566
00:33:42,053 --> 00:33:43,385
Gunshot would draw attention.

567
00:33:45,156 --> 00:33:47,476
The cops will be here soon.
I can make it till they arrive.

568
00:33:47,759 --> 00:33:48,988
SOFIA: James Gordon.

569
00:33:51,997 --> 00:33:54,364
We could've had a
good thing, you and I.

570
00:33:55,901 --> 00:33:59,099
You just had to go and ruin it.

571
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:01,071
Go.

572
00:34:02,073 --> 00:34:03,073
That's an order.

573
00:34:10,382 --> 00:34:11,577
Get Penn.

574
00:34:11,683 --> 00:34:12,844
Get Gordon.

575
00:34:17,188 --> 00:34:19,180
- (ALL EXCLAIMING)
- Get out!

576
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:29,667
(GRUNTS)

577
00:34:31,803 --> 00:34:33,237
- (GRUNTS)
- (GUNSHOT)

578
00:34:33,305 --> 00:34:34,603
(GRUNTS)

579
00:34:38,209 --> 00:34:39,541
(GUN CLICKS)

580
00:34:46,217 --> 00:34:47,810
- (SHELLS CLATTER)
- (GRUNTING)

581
00:34:54,259 --> 00:34:55,557
- (TIRES SCREECH)
- HARVEY: Lee!

582
00:34:56,394 --> 00:34:58,454
- Where's Sofia?
- In there with Jim.

583
00:34:59,230 --> 00:35:02,359
- Take the car.
- He's hurt bad.

584
00:35:02,567 --> 00:35:03,567
Get in.

585
00:35:08,073 --> 00:35:09,803
(TIRES SCREECHING)

586
00:35:14,879 --> 00:35:16,279
(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)

587
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:21,492
Can't catch a break today.

588
00:35:23,054 --> 00:35:24,078
Let's go get a milkshake.

589
00:35:30,929 --> 00:35:32,830
(GRUNTING)

590
00:35:36,368 --> 00:35:38,769
SOFIA: Jim, you really
are such a disappointment.

591
00:35:39,838 --> 00:35:40,931
(GRUNTS)

592
00:35:41,006 --> 00:35:46,274
Would it have been so bad,
being in the palm of my hands,

593
00:35:46,344 --> 00:35:49,212
having me chip away
at your soul little by little?

594
00:35:50,615 --> 00:35:54,882
Was it so important to
rob me of my revenge?

595
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,181
GORDON: That hurt.

596
00:35:57,188 --> 00:35:58,554
- (GUNSHOT)
- (GRUNTS)

597
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:01,683
(GROANING)

598
00:36:01,793 --> 00:36:03,284
It wasn't about me.

599
00:36:04,996 --> 00:36:06,931
I wasn't going to
give you the GCPD.

600
00:36:07,932 --> 00:36:09,525
Of course, it was about you.

601
00:36:10,201 --> 00:36:12,102
Your pride, your arrogance.

602
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:15,306
Do you think that
what I was asking for

603
00:36:15,373 --> 00:36:18,775
was any different than what
my father had for 30 years?

604
00:36:20,945 --> 00:36:22,777
You mean your
father who you killed?

605
00:36:23,882 --> 00:36:24,882
Yes.

606
00:36:25,650 --> 00:36:26,709
I killed him,

607
00:36:28,453 --> 00:36:30,012
because he disappointed me.

608
00:36:31,656 --> 00:36:32,656
Just like you.

609
00:36:36,995 --> 00:36:41,160
You know, Jim, oddly
enough, I still care for you.

610
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:47,536
Beg me for your life.
Ask for forgiveness.

611
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:50,708
And we can start over.

612
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:56,880
Sofia...

613
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:03,420
Go to hell.

614
00:37:11,196 --> 00:37:12,196
SOFIA: James Gordon,

615
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:16,898
this is where our story ends.

616
00:37:19,537 --> 00:37:20,537
(GUNSHOT)

617
00:37:28,346 --> 00:37:29,541
- You.
- Yeah.

618
00:37:31,182 --> 00:37:32,182
Me.

619
00:37:44,395 --> 00:37:45,395
Stay with me, Jim.

620
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,990
(ECHOES) Jim, can you hear me?

621
00:37:53,772 --> 00:37:55,400
(NYGMA LAUGHING)

622
00:37:56,841 --> 00:37:58,104
MAN: Come on, now. Come on.

623
00:38:01,312 --> 00:38:02,552
Hey, I've got a riddle for you.

624
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:05,300
What's got a bullet in its head
and sinks to the bottom of the river?

625
00:38:05,850 --> 00:38:08,012
- You.
- (BOTH LAUGH MANIACALLY)

626
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:09,417
The real torture

627
00:38:10,789 --> 00:38:13,156
is that those idiotic horns
will be the last I ever hear.

628
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:16,284
Just do it!

629
00:38:18,096 --> 00:38:19,792
- (GUNSHOTS)
- (BOTH GRUNT)

630
00:38:24,469 --> 00:38:25,469
Oswald.

631
00:38:27,238 --> 00:38:28,238
How?

632
00:38:29,474 --> 00:38:30,772
Did you already kill Sofia?

633
00:38:32,277 --> 00:38:35,941
No. She left the mansion
to pursue Jim Gordon.

634
00:38:37,348 --> 00:38:38,828
Why didn't you just
stay at the home,

635
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:40,950
wait till she came
there and killed her?

636
00:38:42,287 --> 00:38:43,983
Then I wouldn't have
been here on time.

637
00:38:46,457 --> 00:38:47,982
You gave up your revenge for me?

638
00:38:57,702 --> 00:38:59,637
Trust is so very hard
to find in Gotham.

639
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:03,966
But I trust you, Ed.

640
00:39:27,966 --> 00:39:29,457
I have a strong desire

641
00:39:30,835 --> 00:39:32,963
to never ever
see this pier again.

642
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:35,131
(EXHALES) I agree.

643
00:39:41,512 --> 00:39:43,504
(MONITOR BEEPING STEADILY)

644
00:39:47,919 --> 00:39:48,919
(GASPS)

645
00:39:50,622 --> 00:39:51,622
(GRUNTS)

646
00:39:52,123 --> 00:39:53,421
(SIGHS)

647
00:39:55,193 --> 00:39:56,193
Hey.

648
00:39:57,729 --> 00:39:58,729
Hey.

649
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:00,293
Surprised you're alive?

650
00:40:01,099 --> 00:40:02,362
(GORDON GRUNTS)

651
00:40:03,201 --> 00:40:04,201
Yeah.

652
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,230
- How?
- How do you think?

653
00:40:10,575 --> 00:40:11,575
Lee.

654
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:14,345
She kept you alive till
the medics got there.

655
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,708
Even one-handed,
she's a damn good doctor.

656
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:21,276
- Sofia?
- In a coma.

657
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:23,518
Amazing she's not dead.

658
00:40:31,296 --> 00:40:32,296
Harvey.

659
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,299
When I get out of here,
I'm going to confess.

660
00:40:39,370 --> 00:40:42,807
My connection to Sofia,
my role with the Pyg. All of it.

661
00:40:43,875 --> 00:40:45,036
I gotta come clean.

662
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:47,611
No.

663
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:49,780
What do you mean?

664
00:40:50,648 --> 00:40:52,742
Who would benefit
from that? You.

665
00:40:54,152 --> 00:40:57,520
You get to be the martyr,
feel better about yourself.

666
00:40:58,089 --> 00:41:00,684
The GCPD loses its hero. No!

667
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:03,088
You want to pay your debt?

668
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:05,486
You live with it.

669
00:41:07,532 --> 00:41:08,532
Just like I do.

670
00:41:12,503 --> 00:41:14,131
So, Sofia wins after all?

671
00:41:16,975 --> 00:41:18,238
It's what the city needs.

672
00:41:23,781 --> 00:41:24,781
Where's Lee?

673
00:41:26,250 --> 00:41:27,775
She went back to The Narrows.

674
00:41:28,319 --> 00:41:29,912
Said she had
unfinished business.

675
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:36,291
- (ALL CHEERING)
- (BLOWS LANDING)

676
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:40,770
- MAN 1: Not so tough now.
- Get him!

677
00:41:41,032 --> 00:41:42,472
- Yes! Come on!
- MAN 2: You got him!

678
00:41:44,135 --> 00:41:45,467
(GRUNTING)

679
00:41:48,973 --> 00:41:49,973
SAMPSON: All right.

680
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:53,038
I'll go. I'll go.

681
00:41:53,845 --> 00:41:54,972
Oh, I know you'll go.

682
00:41:56,314 --> 00:41:57,338
Just not yet.

683
00:41:59,751 --> 00:42:00,751
Hold his hand.

684
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:03,187
No. No!

685
00:42:04,489 --> 00:42:05,582
No!

686
00:42:06,090 --> 00:42:08,150
What are you doing? No! No!

687
00:42:08,493 --> 00:42:10,655
(GRUNTS) No!

688
00:42:11,329 --> 00:42:13,355
- (GRUNTS)
- (YELLING IN PAIN)

689
00:42:14,832 --> 00:42:16,164
- (LEE GRUNTS)
- (CROWD CHEERING)

690
00:42:16,234 --> 00:42:17,759
Stop! Don't!

691
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:19,861
- (GRUNTING)
- (SAMPSON YELLING IN PAIN)

692
00:42:23,241 --> 00:42:25,642
("FIRE" PLAYING ON SPEAKERS)

693
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:27,303
(HIGH-PITCHED RINGING)

694
00:42:29,881 --> 00:42:31,076
(GRUNTING)

695
00:42:31,182 --> 00:42:33,293
(MUFFLED) With Sofia gone,
Penguin's gonna try and take control

696
00:42:33,317 --> 00:42:35,343
of Gotham again,
maybe even try and kill us.

697
00:42:35,420 --> 00:42:37,480
Could you just give me a second?

698
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:40,055
Barbara, we have to act.

699
00:42:40,158 --> 00:42:42,439
- We can't just stand around...
- (SHOUTS) I said shut up!

700
00:42:43,327 --> 00:42:44,693
(GASPING)

701
00:42:48,900 --> 00:42:50,562
(SONG CONTINUES PLAYING)
